      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a nice way to put it, but it feels more calculated than just \"human spirit.\" the way the timing works is what bothers me. it's like it's hitting us at our most vulnerable moments. if this was actually a way to test compliance or even just how much discomfort we'll accept for the sake of a trend, what kind of psychological markers would they be looking for? like, if this is a test, what is the actual objective they're trying to measure in people?",
